1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Collecting payments converts accounts receivable into real bank liquidity.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,200
In this session, you will learn how to record customer payment receipts.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,200
Click New Payment Received and select your customer account.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,200
Bill Aura automatically lists all unpaid and partially paid invoices.

5
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,800
Select your deposit bank account and enter the transaction UTR number.

6
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:28,500
Click Auto-Allocate to clear invoices sequentially against the payment.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,400
The invoice status immediately transitions to Paid in bright green.

8
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:38,000
Your bank ledger is debited, and the customer balance clears to zero.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,200
Any excess payment is automatically held as an unallocated customer advance.
